WEBVTT

00:01.951 --> 00:07.211
<b>CITY A</b>

00:01.951 --> 00:07.211
<b>HERO ASSOCIATION HQ</b>

00:05.251 --> 00:09.631
<b>Then it is decided that Mumen Rider will remain the top-ranked hero in Class C.{number one in C-rank}</b>

00:09.631 --> 00:12.761
<b>Understood. We will let him know.</b>

00:12.761 --> 00:17.221
<b>I simply cannot understand why he 
has no desire to move up to Class B…</b>

00:17.641 --> 00:20.431
<b>Next on our agenda is the 
55th Hero Certification Exam.</b>

00:20.431 --> 00:26.611
<b>For this exam, the total number of candidates is…</b>

00:27.361 --> 00:30.741
<b>11,684, with the exam offered at six different venues.</b>

00:31.441 --> 00:34.611
<b>That is an increase of more than 22% over the previous exam{she actually uses "tournament" instead of "exam"}.{regardless it doesn't look much like a tournament}</b>

00:37.031 --> 00:39.411
<b>We mustn't be satisfied with merely a higher quantity.{happy with simple quantity.}</b>

00:39.911 --> 00:41.621
<b>Even with more candidates,</b>

00:41.621 --> 00:46.081
<b>if the quality of the heroes is reduced, the numbers are meaningless.</b>

00:48.711 --> 00:52.801
<b>Therefore, we ought to be even 
more critical during evaluations.</b>

00:52.801 --> 00:58.301
<b>Also, I hear that a certain person of interest 
is taking the exam this time.</b>

00:58.301 --> 01:01.311
<b>Yes, it hasn't been confirmed yet,</b>

01:01.931 --> 01:05.231
<b>but it seems very likely that he will.</b>

